   "t": 55.25,
   "kind": "thought",
   "data": {
    "text": "In a `120 mm / 3 h` storm the Lekki-Epe Expressway is not passable without interventions.\n\nBaseline run `r_3277ec9d2e6e1ec8`:\n\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:road_km_impassable` = 36.515 km\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:max_depth_m` = 1.185 m\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:flooded_area_km2` = 0.8484\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:buildings_flooded` = 769\n\nPassability threshold in model = 0.3 m. `max_depth_m > 0.3` and `road_km_impassable > 0` = impassable.\n\nTested one change at a time vs baseline:\n\n**1 intervention: city-wide new drainage `add_mm_h: 40`**\nRun `r_f0d5c0524f2f2b6f` - described as city-wide new drainage, not a local fix.\n\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:road_km_impassable` = 3.6 km\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:max_depth_m` = 0.473 m\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:flooded_area_km2` = 0.1859\n* Whole area: `buildings_flooded` 30202 -> 12550, `road_km_impassable` 406.713 -> 31.733 km\n\nLarge reduction, but Expressway still impassable: 3.6 km > 0 and 0.473 m > 0.3 m.\n\n**2 interventions: city-wide `capacity_factor:3.0 + add_mm_h:40` + green in Lekki Phase 1**\nRun `r_c1a9ed4c5e29725d`:\n\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:road_km_impassable` = 2.278 km\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:max_depth_m` = 0.473 m\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:flooded_area_km2` = 0.1142\n* Whole area: `buildings_flooded` 30202 -> 11453, `road_km_impassable` 406.713 -> 26.903 km\n\nBetter than 1-intervention, but still not passable.\n\nPond on `Open land near Ajah` tested in combination triggered simulator warning: ponds cover buildings. Per planning rules that scenario is invalid and cannot be counted as flood reduction.\n\nConclusion:\n\nNo tested set achieves `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:road_km_impassable = 0` with `max_depth_m < 0.3 m`.\n\nSmallest / most effective valid set tested is the 2-part set above, and it still leaves 2.278 km impassable on the Expressway at 0.473 m max depth.\n\nKeeping the Expressway fully passable in 120 mm / 3 h will require measures beyond what could be confirmed within the 4-run budget.\n"
   }
